  "response": "<issues>\n- If `df` does not have a DatetimeIndex (e.g., uses a default RangeIndex), `seasonal_decompose` will raise a `ValueError` from statsmodels because it cannot infer the frequency/period. We must assign a default DatetimeIndex aligned with `freq` when one is missing.\n- `asfreq(freq)` can introduce missing values (`NaN`s) if the original DatetimeIndex has gaps or misaligned dates, which will subsequently cause `seasonal_decompose` to crash. Missing values must be filled (e.g., using `ffill().bfill()`).\n- The code does not recognize `pd.PeriodIndex` as a valid time series index, which is another standard index type that supports `asfreq` and is acceptable for decomposition.\n</issues>\n<solution>\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom statsmodels.tsa.seasonal import seasonal_decompose\n\ndef task_func(df, freq='D', decomposition_model='multiplicative'):\n    # Validate DataFrame\n    if not isinstance(df, pd.DataFrame) or 'value' not in df.columns or not pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(df['value']):\n        raise ValueError(\"If 'df' is not a DataFrame, lacks required columns, or contains invalid data types.\")\n        \n    # Validate frequency string\n    try:\n        pd.date_range(start='2020-01-01', periods=2, freq=freq)\n    except Exception:\n        raise ValueError(\"If 'freq' is not a valid frequency string.\")\n        \n    # Validate decomposition model\n    if decomposition_model not in ['additive', 'multiplicative']:\n        raise ValueError(\"If 'decomposition_model' is not 'additive' or 'multiplicative'.\")\n\n    # Prepare time series\n    series = df['value'].copy()\n    if isinstance(series.index, (pd.DatetimeIndex, pd.PeriodIndex)):\n        series = series.asfreq(freq)\n    else:\n        # Assign a default DatetimeIndex with the provided frequency for dataframes without one\n        series.index = pd.date_range(start='2020-01-01', periods=len(series), freq=freq)\n        \n    # seasonal_decompose does not handle NaNs in the middle of the series; \n    # asfreq() or missing original data might introduce NaNs.\n    if series.isna().any():\n        series = series.ffill().bfill()\n        \n    # Perform decomposition\n    result = seasonal_decompose(series, model=decomposition_model)\n    \n    # Plot and extract Axes\n    fig = result.plot()\n    ax = fig.axes[0] if fig.axes else plt.gca()\n    \n    return result, ax\n</solution>",
